# ---------- Secrets / local config ----------
# The repository-root .env is COMMITTED on purpose: it carries the PostgreSQL
# database name and password for the EC2 deployment, so that only the five
# AWS/Docker Hub secrets have to live in GitHub. Anything added to it is
# visible to everyone who can read this repository.
.env
!/.env

# Every other .env stays ignored: .env.local for a developer's own overrides,
# and .env.ci, which the pipeline generates on the runner from GitHub secrets.
.env.*

appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json

